{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And the meaning of \"this one will comfort us\":</b> he knew through Adam, for he was a prophet, that through this one being born the ground would live, or they saw this by way of wisdom. And so it was, for through him the world was sustained. He too was a man of the ground, for so it is written. It is also possible that he was named Noah as Jerubbaal was named, after he worked the ground and it succeeded, and Noah is the reverse of sorrow — \"and the meaning: this one will comfort us, and we will rest from the sorrow of our hands\" — also comfort is rest from sorrow of the heart, for the Hebrews preserve the meanings and not the words. The proof is Jeresheth and Jerubbaal. Those who ask who was the wife of Cain or of Seth — what is the point of this question, for it is written of Adam that he begot sons and daughters, and so for all of them."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:26.775581754Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}